 31S  c  2025BuAA: {+31}Cl was produced by the fragmentation of a 150           
 31S 2c  MeV/nucleon {+36}Ar beam on a 1645 mg/cm{+2} Be primary target,        
 31S 3c  separated and purified by the A1900 fragment separator and the Radio   
 31S 4c  Frequency Fragment Separator (RFFS), and transported into the Proton   
 31S 5c  Detector (PD) of the Gaseous Detector with Germanium Tagging (GADGET)  
 31S 6c  system surrounded by the SeGA array of 16 HPGe detectors. Measured     
 31S 7c  E{-p}, I{-p}, and p|g-coin. Deduced levels, |e+|b{++}-decay branching  
 31S 8c  ratios, log {Ift}, and B(GT), and compared with shell-model            
 31S 9c  calculations.                                                          
